|* Post-layout sampler_dff: capture timing, output levels and the
|* reset-window / idle / active supply currents of the raw-tap digitizer,
|* extracted parasitics vs. the pre-layout netlist, in ONE deck.
|*
|* Purpose. Two named, still-open items meet here:
|*
|*   1. issue #22 acceptance criterion 2 -- post-layout PVT simulation over
|*      extracted parasitics. Every post-layout record this repo holds so far
|*      (sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/, -ro-ring5-assembled/, -ro-array-core/) is
|*      on the ENTROPY SOURCE side of the raw tap. The sampler has none: no
|*      sim/ record anywhere measures sampler_dff at all, pre- or
|*      post-layout.
|*   2. DR-0003's own "Follow-up required" list -- "**Sampler_dff
|*      characterization** for the now six-instance-per-block liveness/raw-tap
|*      digitizer fan-out (unsimulated, per design/xschem/trng_top.sch's own
|*      text block)". This deck is the first measurement of that cell.
|*
|* and one methodology transfer spec/porting-plan.md asks for explicitly:
|* DR-0014 (gf180-trng, Accepted/delegated) chose to gate sampler_dff's
|* asynchronous reset into the storage loops' own inverters rather than hang
|* pull devices on the storage nodes, on the strength of a *measured*
|* reset-window contention current (967 uW -> 66 nW on gf180mcu). The
|* porting plan is explicit that "the **methodology** -- measure reset-window
|* contention current explicitly, per the specific storage-loop topology
|* chosen, before assuming a brute-force reset is 'free' -- transfers; the
|* **specific gating arrangement and its polarity argument does not". So the
|* number is re-derived here on sky130, on this repo's own drawn topology,
|* rather than transplanted. i_rst_* below is that measurement.
|*
|* Why both DFFs are in ONE deck rather than compared across two records.
|* Same argument sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/'s own header makes: the quantity
|* of interest is a RATIO (how much slower is the same cell once its own
|* intra-cell parasitics are present), and a ratio taken across two runs
|* silently inherits every difference between them -- corner section,
|* temperature, solver settings, ngspice build, stimulus edge rate. Running
|* the pre-layout cell as a same-deck control on the same stimulus sources
|* makes the parasitics the ONLY thing that differs between the two numbers.
|*
|* Topology. design/sampler_core.spice's `.subckt sampler_dff` is FLAT --
|* 22 devices, no sub-instances, because design/xschem/sampler_dff.sch has no
|* sub-schematic symbol for an inverter, a transmission gate or a NAND2. The
|* post-layout side below rebuilds those same 22 devices as the nine composed
|* leaf-cell instances layout/sampler_dff/ physically places:
|*
|*   3 x sampler_inv_pex    layout/ro_buf/         XMpc/XMnc, XMim2p/XMim2n,
|*                                                 XMisp/XMisn
|*   4 x sampler_tg_pex     layout/sampler_tg/     TG_D, TG_FBM, TG_S, TG_FBS
|*   2 x sampler_nand2_pex  layout/sampler_nand2/  NAND_M, NAND_S2
|*
|* wired per design/sampler_core.spice device for device (see the
|* sampler_dff_pex subcircuit below, whose every port assignment is annotated
|* with the design device it reproduces). Each of those three cells is `klt
|* drc` clean (0 violations) and `klt lvs` matching its own reference
|* netlist; layout/pex/pex-sampler.json extracts all three with
|* `klt extract --parasitics` into layout/pex/sampler_dff_pex.spice.
|*
|* WHAT THIS IS NOT. This is intra-cell parasitics only, plus IDEAL
|* inter-cell wires -- exactly the scope sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/ has for
|* the ring, and one level below sim/post-layout-ro-ring5-assembled/'s
|* whole-GDS extraction. layout/sampler_dff/'s own assembly (placement +
|* vdd/vss buses + the routed rst_n/clk/clkb/mc/q/qb/s nets) exists and is
|* DRC-clean, but its `m`/`mb` data-path nets are still unrouted and its
|* `klt lvs` does not match yet (see layout/sampler_dff/README.md and issue
|* #84), so extracting THAT GDS flat would extract an incomplete circuit.
|* Every number below is therefore a floor on the real post-layout cost, not
|* the whole of it.
|*
|* Stimulus is ideal (PWL sources, 100 ps edges), identical for both sides.
|* That is deliberate for a fair pre-vs-post ratio -- both cells see the same
|* edge -- but it also means the post-layout cell's larger input capacitance
|* does not slow its own clk/d edges the way a real driver would. Another
|* reason to read these as a floor.
|*
|* The waveform (ns), one full reset -> idle -> capture-1 -> capture-0 cycle:
|*
|*    0 .. 25   rst_n = 0, clk = 0, d = 1   reset asserted WHILE the data
|*                                          input drives the opposite value
|*                                          through the transparent master --
|*                                          the condition under which a
|*                                          brute-force pull-device reset
|*                                          would fight the d driver, i.e.
|*                                          DR-0014's contention case.
|*                                          i_rst_* measured over 15..25 ns.
|*   25 .. 45   rst_n = 1, clk = 0, d = 1   idle, quiescent. i_idle_*
|*                                          measured over 35..45 ns.
|*   50         clk 0 -> 1                  rising edge captures d = 1.
|*                                          tcq_rise_* = clk -> q delay.
|*   60         clk 1 -> 0
|*   70         d 1 -> 0                    master follows (clk = 0), slave
|*                                          holds -- q must NOT move here.
|*   80         clk 0 -> 1                  rising edge captures d = 0.
|*                                          tcq_fall_* = clk -> q delay.
|*   90         clk 1 -> 0
|*
|* This cell is rising-edge triggered: TG_D conducts on clk = 0 (XMtdp's
|* gate is clk, XMtdn's is clkb) so the master is transparent LOW, and TG_S
|* conducts on clk = 1 so the slave is transparent HIGH.
|*
|* The substrate tie. layout/pex/sampler_dff_pex.spice declares the
|* extractor's substrate return node `vsubs` .global (klayout-tools#1503).
|* This deck ties it HARD to 0, the same physically-motivated choice
|* sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/'s primary deck makes: every composed cell here
|* carries its own psub guard ring tied to vss, and vss is 0 in this deck.
|*
|* PVT: run at the same four (temp, supply) points every post-layout campaign
|* in this repo uses, each bundling the tt/ss/ff process axis into one record:
|*   -40 degC / 1.62 V   the measured entropy-binding corner (ss)
|*    27 degC / 1.80 V   nominal
|*   125 degC / 1.98 V   hottest/fastest
|*   -40 degC / 1.98 V   coldest/fastest
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /home/ubuntu/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* ss, /home/ubuntu/loom-workspaces/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/design/sampler_core.spice (pointed at design/sampler_core.spice for this
|* deck), /home/ubuntu/loom-workspaces/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex/sampler_dff_pex.spice (pointed at layout/pex/sampler_dff_pex.spice), 125.0,
|* 1.98 and 5p. As committed it is not a runnable deck.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/home/ubuntu/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" ss
|
|* pre-layout subcircuit library -- design/sampler_core.spice, which carries
|* both the flat `.subckt sampler_dff` under test and the `.subckt ro_buf`
|* used as its output load on the pre-layout side.
|.include "/home/ubuntu/loom-workspaces/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/design/sampler_core.spice"
|* post-layout subcircuit library (sampler_*_pex), generated from layout/
|.include "/home/ubuntu/loom-workspaces/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex/sampler_dff_pex.spice"
|
|.temp 125.0
|
|* --- substrate return node: hard tie (see header) ----------------------
|Vsub vsubs 0 dc 0
|
|*-----------------------------------------------------------------------
|* The post-layout sampler_dff, assembled from extracted leaf cells.
|*
|* Port order and net names are design/sampler_core.spice's own, so the two
|* instantiations further down differ by one token. Each line names the
|* design devices it reproduces.
|*-----------------------------------------------------------------------
|.subckt sampler_dff_pex d clk rst_n q vdd vss
|* clk inverter                              XMpc  / XMnc
|xinv_clk clk    clkb   vdd vss           sampler_inv_pex
|* input transmission gate, on when clk=0    XMtdp / XMtdn
|xtg_d    d      m      clk  clkb vdd vss sampler_tg_pex
|* master forward inverter, rst_n-gated      XMimpa/XMimpb/XMimna/XMimnb
|xnand_m  m      rst_n  mb   vdd  vss     sampler_nand2_pex
|* master feedback inverter                  XMim2p / XMim2n
|xinv_mc  mb     mc     vdd vss           sampler_inv_pex
|* master feedback gate, on when clk=1       XMfmp / XMfmn
|xtg_fbm  mc     m      clkb clk  vdd vss sampler_tg_pex
|* slave input gate, on when clk=1           XMtsp / XMtsn
|xtg_s    mb     s      clkb clk  vdd vss sampler_tg_pex
|* slave forward inverter                    XMisp / XMisn
|xinv_q   s      q      vdd vss           sampler_inv_pex
|* slave feedback inverter, rst_n-gated      XMis2pa/XMis2pb/XMis2na/XMis2nb
|xnand_s2 q      rst_n  qb   vdd  vss     sampler_nand2_pex
|* slave feedback gate, on when clk=0        XMfsp / XMfsn
|xtg_fbs  qb     s      clk  clkb vdd vss sampler_tg_pex
|.ends
|
|* --- shared stimulus, identical for both sides -------------------------
|* clk: low through reset and idle, then two rising edges at 50 ns and 80 ns.
|Vclk clk 0 PWL(0 0  50n 0  50.1n 1.98  60n 1.98  60.1n 0
|+ 80n 0  80.1n 1.98  90n 1.98  90.1n 0)
|* rst_n: asserted (low) for the first 25 ns, released thereafter.
|Vrstn rst_n 0 PWL(0 0  25n 0  25.1n 1.98)
|* d: high across reset (the contention condition -- see header), falling at
|* 70 ns while the master is transparent so the second edge captures a 0.
|Vd d 0 PWL(0 1.98  70n 1.98  70.1n 0)
|
|* --- the two DFFs under test, one supply source each --------------------
|Vddp vddp 0 dc 1.98
|xdp d clk rst_n qp vddp 0 sampler_dff_pex
|Vddq vddq 0 dc 1.98
|xdq d clk rst_n qq vddq 0 sampler_dff
|
|* --- output load: one inverter per side, on its own supply --------------
|* design/sampler_core.spice taps q into the digital section; loading both
|* sides identically (post-layout inverter on the post-layout DFF,
|* pre-layout inverter on the pre-layout DFF) keeps the comparison fair
|* without letting the load's own current contaminate either DFF's supply.
|Vddl vddl 0 dc 1.98
|xlp qp qpb vddl 0 sampler_inv_pex
|xlq qq qqb vddl 0 ro_buf
|
|.tran 5p 100n
|
|.control
|run
|
|* --- capture timing: clk -> q, both directions -------------------------
|* First clk rising edge (50 ns) captures d = 1; second (80 ns) captures
|* d = 0. Measured at the 50% crossing on both signals.
|meas tran tcq_rise_pex TRIG v(clk) VAL='0.5*1.98' RISE=1
|+ TARG v(qp) VAL='0.5*1.98' RISE=1
|meas tran tcq_rise_pre TRIG v(clk) VAL='0.5*1.98' RISE=1
|+ TARG v(qq) VAL='0.5*1.98' RISE=1
|meas tran tcq_fall_pex TRIG v(clk) VAL='0.5*1.98' RISE=2
|+ TARG v(qp) VAL='0.5*1.98' FALL=1
|meas tran tcq_fall_pre TRIG v(clk) VAL='0.5*1.98' RISE=2
|+ TARG v(qq) VAL='0.5*1.98' FALL=1
|
|* The headline ratios: same cell, same corner, same stimulus, parasitics
|* on vs. off.
|let slowdown_tcq_rise = tcq_rise_pex / tcq_rise_pre
|let slowdown_tcq_fall = tcq_fall_pex / tcq_fall_pre
|
|* --- captured levels: is the post-layout cell functionally correct? -----
|* After the 50 ns edge q must be a solid 1 and hold it through the 70 ns
|* d transition (the slave is opaque then); after the 80 ns edge a solid 0.
|* Worst case within each hold window, so a droop or a glitch shows up.
|meas tran vq_hi_pex MIN v(qp) from=55n to=79n
|meas tran vq_hi_pre MIN v(qq) from=55n to=79n
|meas tran vq_lo_pex MAX v(qp) from=85n to=100n
|meas tran vq_lo_pre MAX v(qq) from=85n to=100n
|let vq_hi_frac_pex = vq_hi_pex / 1.98
|let vq_hi_frac_pre = vq_hi_pre / 1.98
|let vq_lo_frac_pex = vq_lo_pex / 1.98
|let vq_lo_frac_pre = vq_lo_pre / 1.98
|
|* Reset must hold q at 0 while d drives the opposite value.
|meas tran vq_rst_pex MAX v(qp) from=15n to=25n
|meas tran vq_rst_pre MAX v(qq) from=15n to=25n
|
|* --- supply current: reset window, idle, active ------------------------
|* i(Vsrc) is negative for current delivered by the source, so every printed
|* figure is sign-flipped to read as consumed current.
|* i_rst_*  : DR-0014's contention measurement, re-derived for sky130 on
|*            this repo's own storage-loop topology (see header).
|* i_idle_* : quiescent current with the clock stopped low, reset released.
|* i_act_*  : average over the whole two-edge capture sequence.
|meas tran irstp AVG i(Vddp) from=15n to=25n
|meas tran irstq AVG i(Vddq) from=15n to=25n
|meas tran iidlp AVG i(Vddp) from=35n to=45n
|meas tran iidlq AVG i(Vddq) from=35n to=45n
|meas tran iactp AVG i(Vddp) from=45n to=100n
|meas tran iactq AVG i(Vddq) from=45n to=100n
|let i_rst_pex = -irstp
|let i_rst_pre = -irstq
|let i_idle_pex = -iidlp
|let i_idle_pre = -iidlq
|let i_act_pex = -iactp
|let i_act_pre = -iactq
|
|print tcq_rise_pex
|print tcq_rise_pre
|print tcq_fall_pex
|print tcq_fall_pre
|print slowdown_tcq_rise
|print slowdown_tcq_fall
|print vq_hi_frac_pex
|print vq_hi_frac_pre
|print vq_lo_frac_pex
|print vq_lo_frac_pre
|print vq_rst_pex
|print vq_rst_pre
|print i_rst_pex
|print i_rst_pre
|print i_idle_pex
|print i_idle_pre
|print i_act_pex
|print i_act_pre
|.endc
|.end
|

